@startuml
title logGO - Ingestion Sequence (internal/ingest.Run, one per PULL source)

participant "internal/sources.Registry" as Registry
participant "ingest.Run" as Run
participant "remote instance\nGET /logs" as REST
participant "remote instance\nGET /ws/logs" as WS
participant "logGO.Manager\n(this instance)" as Manager

Registry -> Run: go Run(ctx, opts, manager)\n(spawned by Registry.start —\nonce at boot per persisted source,\nor immediately on a runtime Add;\nctx canceled by Registry.Remove)
activate Run

== Initial backfill: existing history ==
Run -> REST: GET /logs?since=<zero> (X-API-Key: opts.APIKey)
REST --> Run: [] remoteEntry{timestamp, level, message, fields}
loop for each entry
  Run -> Run: NewEntry(ts, level, message, fields + source tag)
  Run -> Manager: WriteEntry(entry)
  note right: preserves the entry's own\ntimestamp -- NOT time.Now(),\nunlike WriteLog
end
Run -> Run: lastSeen = newest timestamp seen

== Live tail: everything new from here on ==
Run -> WS: Dial ws(s)://.../ws/logs?api_key=...
activate WS
loop until disconnect or ctx canceled
  WS --> Run: one JSON message per new entry
  Run -> Manager: WriteEntry(entry)
  Run -> Run: lastSeen = entry.timestamp
end
WS --> Run: read error (connection dropped)
deactivate WS

== Reconnect, with backoff and gap-refill ==
Run -> Manager: WriteLog("WARN", "disconnected, retrying")
Run -> Run: sleep(backoff); backoff = min(backoff*2, 30s)
Run -> REST: GET /logs?since=lastSeen\n(catch anything missed while disconnected)
REST --> Run: [] remoteEntry (the gap)
loop for each entry
  Run -> Manager: WriteEntry(entry)
end
Run -> Run: backoff reset to 1s
Run -> WS: Dial again (back to "Live tail" above)

== Ends when the source is removed (not just on process shutdown) ==
Registry -> Run: ctx canceled (Registry.Remove(id), or process shutdown)
Run --> Registry: return ctx.Err()
deactivate Run

note over Registry, Manager
  This is PULL — logGO connecting out to a
  registered source. The inverse, PUSH (a
  client sending straight to logGO over REST/
  WebSocket/gRPC), is a separate, unrelated
  code path — see 06-push-ingestion-sequence.puml.
  Both end up tagging entries with a "source"
  field and calling the same Manager.WriteEntry.
end note

@enduml
